From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:59:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: stmpe: normalize block read results

The STMPE SPI callback returns zero after filling the requested buffer,
while the I2C callback currently returns the transferred byte count. The
common API therefore cannot distinguish I2C zero-byte and short
transfers from SPI success.

Normalize I2C full-length success to zero and reject every nonnegative
short transfer with -EIO. Preserve negative errors and the existing SPI
convention, document the common zero-success contract, and avoid dumping
or consuming buffers after a failed read. Update the two existing
consumers which ignored block-read failures.

Add transport-level KUnit coverage for I2C counts zero through four,
exact-length success, negative error propagation, and a zero-returning
SPI callback which fills the complete buffer.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
